# Maze of Ith prevents a creature's combat damage as it is dealt, not its assignment (CR 510.1-2, 615.1): the creature stays
# blocked (the rulings), so a trampler still assigns lethal damage to its blocker before any reaches the player (CR 702.19b).
# Bot1's Ulvenwald Oddity (4/4 trample, haste) attacks; Bot2's Llanowar Elves blocks; Bot2 Mazes the Oddity after blocks.
# Bot1 still divides its 4 - 1 to the Elves (lethal), 3 to Bot2 - and every point of it is prevented, as is the Elves' 1
# to the Oddity. Bot2 stays at 20 and the Elves live.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Ulvenwald Oddity
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Maze of Ith
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Maze of Ith.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ulvenwald Oddity.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Ulvenwald Oddity > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Ulvenwald Oddity)
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Maze of Ith.Activate(Ulvenwald Oddity)
Bot1.AssignDamage(Ulvenwald Oddity > Llanowar Elves: 1; Ulvenwald Oddity > Bot2: 3)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Damage = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ulvenwald Oddity.Damage = 0
Prevented = 1 Ulvenwald Oddity > Llanowar Elves by Maze of Ith; 3 Ulvenwald Oddity > Bot2 by Maze of Ith; 1 Llanowar Elves > Ulvenwald Oddity by Maze of Ith
